// slice-entry: json_valid json_find json_type_at json_num_at
// JSON for our tools, in Omega. This is the parse half of every wrapped
// binary we are replacing (gh speaks JSON on every call). One pass, no
// recursion: the container stack is the caller's cells, 1 = object, 2 =
// array, st[1..top]. Depth past the stack refuses. Strings honor the
// escapes the spec allows and refuse every other one. Numbers follow the
// grammar: -? (0 | [1-9][0-9]*) (. digits+)? ([eE] [+-]? digits+)?.
// json_find locates a key's value offset and never matches a key inside a
// string value, because strings are consumed whole. json_num_at reads a
// plain nonnegative integer and refuses anything with a sign, a fraction
// or an exponent. Offsets in the run lines are Wolfram-derived.
